980	    /** Days past its due date an invoice is given before it becomes overdue: a week's grace. */
981	    public static final int GRACE_DAYS = 7;
982	
983	    /**
984	     * The status on the given day once the given amount has been paid against the grand total at the
985	     * tax rate: a sent invoice with something still due more than {@link #GRACE_DAYS} days after its
986	     * due date is overdue, part paid or not. Held retention is never due, so never makes it overdue;
987	     * released retention is due {@link #RETENTION_DUE_DAYS} days after its release, and payments go to
988	     * the rest of the invoice before it. An invoice spread over instalments is instead overdue when any
989	     * of its instalments is (see {@link #instalmentProgress}).
990	     */
991	    public InvoiceStatus statusWhenPaid(BigDecimal paid, BigDecimal taxRate, LocalDate today) {
